From ec3434bbc93fd54d69e39e43c0327fcf144d1821 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:25:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/25] Shaders: ds_bpermute_b32 across two host waves through
 a table past the LDS

A console wave64 program run as two host waves of 32 stopped at the
checkerboard shadow-mask generators' neighbour read ("a lane permute
across two host waves"): the pair of exchange dwords cannot carry every
lane's dword. Each console wave of the group now gets 64 table dwords
past the exchange dwords; every lane stores its own (a lane its guard
holds off stores 0, as the console reads for a source lane outside EXEC),
the halves meet on a group barrier, and the read takes the named lane's
dword from it. Where not every lane runs the block, the lowering refuses
as before and names it for the wave-wide retry.

The write-up's five shadow-mask trace programs are expected to translate
now; verified through the tests (lowering on every host, values on a
32-lane card when one runs the suite).

(cherry picked from commit 2a40b4803fd5b558cf523166ae47a43981e859b8)
(cherry picked from commit 186f3ac7769d332d16e4b7dd8c9cc4dee4725aec)
